# E-Commerce Overlay

- Prices are integer minor units with a currency code. Taxes, discounts, and shipping are separate line items computed server-side.
- Snapshot price, tax, and product title onto the order line at purchase time; never recompute historical orders from the live catalog.
- Orders follow an explicit state machine: `pending -> paid -> fulfilled -> delivered`, with `canceled` and `refunded` branches.
- Reserve inventory with an expiring reservation at checkout; commit on payment success and release on timeout or cancel.
- Payment calls use idempotency keys. Confirm payment from the provider webhook, not from the client redirect.
- Never handle raw card data. Use hosted fields or provider tokens to stay out of PCI scope.
- Cart totals shown in the client are advisory; the server recalculates and validates on checkout.
- Emit telemetry for `cart.item_added`, `checkout.started`, `checkout.completed`, `order.refunded`.
